{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/390048-2e-thoughts-do-we-need-the-vulnerability-to-fire","id":390048,"title":"[2e Thoughts] Do we need the vulnerability to fire?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-02T10:32:06-08:00","id":390048,"title":"[2e Thoughts] Do we need the vulnerability to fire?","content":"This isn't a powerful/not powerful argument, just a thematic one. The vulnerability to fire is mentioned once in the Promethean corebook, but never seems to really come up in the fiction and certainly doesn't seem to carry the same level of mythic resonance that &quot;fire-as-bane&quot; does for Vampires and Mummies. The explanation of the Promethean's alchemical chemistry reacting badly to fire isn't all that deep or well-explained. It seems almost entirely forgotten about in the supplements and feels a little bit unnecessary to me. That line in the corebook could have been omitted by accident and I doubt anyone would have noticed. <br /> <br /> I know it's a Frankenstein &quot;Fire Bad!&quot; reference, but I guess I question it's necessity and thematic value to the game. Prometheans don't get appreciably that much more powerful taking lethal damage from fire rather than aggravated; they're still basically vulnerable to anything a mortal is vulnerable to, they just have to take more punishment before it starts to really hurt. They can be shot in the head, strangled, suffocated, starved, run over with a truck, etc. They can take a lot of punishment, but part of the Promethean theme is endurance (it's the &quot;Resistance&quot; game, after all) which is somewhat undermined by a relatively common threat they cannot endure in the slightest. <br /> <br /> I don't think that Prometheans need any specific bane (though something with a real basis in folklore or alchemy might work); they're already supposed to be bloody tough, but they aren't (at present) insurmountably so even without the use of fire, fire at lethal is still pretty damn dangerous, and I don't necessarily see the thematic value of avoiding fire (more than you'd avoid any lethal damage, mind you) that exists for Vampires and Mummies. I think the theme of Promethean is supported by the idea you can't put one down with any kind of specific weakness, like a silver bullet or fire, but with overwhelming force - they don't give up their Pilgrimage easily, but the forces arrayed against them (Disquiet, torch-and-pitchfork bearing mobs, etc) are overwhelming. <br /> <br /> Just a thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T14:25:12-08:00","id":390351,"title":"","content":"I have to say, I agree with this.<br /> <br /> I think it might've been to make the torches more dangerous... but that's a silly justification now that I think of it (which means that it probably isn't the actual reason.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T14:25:57-08:00","id":390358,"title":"","content":"In all the games I've been in involving Prometheans we dropped the &quot;Fire Bad!&quot; rule for reasons similar to what you outlined. It makes sense for Mummies and Vampires as, yeah, they're corpses, and corpses dry out and turn into kindling. Prometheans aren't undead or undying, but rather &quot;unalive&quot;. Their tissues aren't desiccated, and mimic many biological functions.<br /> <br /> Further, if you build a Promethean using the Construct rules and, say, make a Galatead out of marble, Fire Bad makes even less sense. Same goes for most Unfleshed. Naturally if your Promethean was made out of wood or some other flammable material it <i>should</i> apply.<br /> <br /> At the same time it's one of those rules that's pretty easy to excise. I believe it only effects two other rules: 1) it would remove a Torment trigger and 2) the Sublimate Phlogoston Transmutation in Vulcanus would be <i>slightly </i>different. I imagine it also makes Pandorans a little tougher too but I can't recall offhand if they vulnerable to fire or not (they likely are).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","user":"Metamurpho","date":". 02-02-2015, 07:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T14:55:21-08:00","id":390411,"title":"","content":"The original core book started off with everyone being a Frankenstein monster. Which was quickly moved away from in pretty much every book past that. Now, we have Unfleshed, alternate methods made from clay or marble, and so on.<br /> <br /> So, no, fire doesn't make sense in the modern times. I think there should be SOME bane out there. I feel it should be in every game line. Just not fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T14:57:07-08:00","id":390413,"title":"","content":"What, Disquiet + Wasteland not enough of a Bane for you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T01:49:33-08:00","id":391156,"title":"","content":"It's something of a supernatural rule in nWoD that &quot;dead things&quot; - Vampires, Prometheans, Mummies - are all vulnerable to fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T02:19:45-08:00","id":391171,"title":"","content":"Vampires have a \u201cmost damage I take is bashing\u201d thing going for them; making fire an exception to that is rather important. I <i>think</i> the same holds true for mummies and zombies. <br /> <br /> But Prometheans aren\u2019t like that, necessarily: they may not be \u201cdead things\u201d. They eat and breathe, and I wouldn\u2019t be surprised to learn that they have a pulse. Arguably, they shouldn\u2019t benefit from \u201call damage is bashing\u201d: unlike the undead, it\u2019s entirely possible that their internal organs actually <i>do something</i> \u2014 though probably not what they would do if the Promethean was human. For instance, the stomache digests food \u2014 but in the case of a Promethean, this \u201cdigestion\u201d is more of a metaphysical furnace feeding the Azoth that drives the Promethean. The lungs probably work in a similar way, feeding the Fire instead of oxygenating the blood. In effect, a Promethean\u2019s body is an intricate alchemical engine that drives its ongoing animation; and if any of its parts get damaged, that likely throws the alchemical reactions out of whack. So swords and bullets do lethal rather than bashing. <br /> <br /> If this is so, then special vulnerability to fire isn\u2019t appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T04:27:29-08:00","id":391243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/390048-2e-thoughts-do-we-need-the-vulnerability-to-fire?p=390413#post390413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What, Disquiet + Wasteland not enough of a Bane for you?</div> </div> </div> </div> We don't know what Disquiet and Wasteland will be like going forwards. And, to be honest, I feel that neither of those is really a bane. Its a plot point to encourage the theme of Pilgrimage on the Promethean. Its more akin to the vampire's social penalties for having low Humanity, ramped up.<br /> <br /> Banes are something that is anathema to the supernatural. It unravels its very nature, and is primarily used offensively (often combat, but not always) against them. Iron used to contain one of the fae, fire to destroy the vampire's blood magics, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/390048-2e-thoughts-do-we-need-the-vulnerability-to-fire?p=391156#post391156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's something of a supernatural rule in nWoD that &quot;dead things&quot; - Vampires, Prometheans, Mummies - are all vulnerable to fire.</div> </div> </div> </div> Major undead templates, yes. It should be noted that zombies made from mage-magic aren't. Nor are ghosts. So, that's not an absolute rule.<br /> <br /> In either case, considering that Prometheans' own books, as well as Book of the Dead, ranks the Prometheans as living beings instead of undead, its a moot point. To use D&amp;D terms, Prometheans are constructs and golems. The game covers magical (and occult science-y) Creations.<br /> <br /> Vampires, mummies, strix, and some zombies are all described as running off some kind of Curse. Its the tag line of Mummy, and a recurring theme running in Vampire alongside the word Damned. Fire is the bane of the cursed undead. Ghosts, geister, and Bound/Sin-Eaters aren't cursed, even as they all run off ectoplasm; their banes are fluid, depending on the individual ban (yes, Bound get bans and banes via their krewes). Prometheans are constructs (possibly flesh, but not necessarily) powered by the divine fire. Why should Created have a ban? They don't have spirit connections, they don't run off a Curse.<br /> <br /> Thematically, Frankenstein's monster was scared of fire. Fair enough. Franky has a lot in common with zombies. The golem, however, wasn't - his weakness was someone marring the True Name inscribed on his forehead (mage?). Osiris has much in common with the death-gods of GtSE and the Underworld, who are more likely to be weak to salt than fire. The legend of Galatea didn't involve killing her or chasing her with flames; on a related legend of Creepy Dolls, fire isn't as often a solution when compared to a sledgehammer. Unfleshed might come from robots - their &quot;classical weakness&quot; is electricity or someone hacking and reprogramming. <br /> <br /> And so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-03-2015, 07:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T08:33:46-08:00","id":391458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/390048-2e-thoughts-do-we-need-the-vulnerability-to-fire?p=391243#post391243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Banes are something that is anathema to the supernatural. It unravels its very nature, and is primarily used offensively (often combat, but not always) against them. Iron used to contain one of the fae, fire to destroy the vampire's blood magics, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes me think that if Prometheans have a bane, it ought to be something that stifles the alchemy inside them, rather than doing harm per se. In game terms, leeching Pyros rather than doing damage.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T08:47:25-08:00","id":391471,"title":"","content":"There is also the point that, of course Frankenstein's monster was afraid of fire. Fire burns. That shit hurts. Even if you are not <i>especially </i>combustible it still deals lethal damage to regular people. Why wouldn't he be afraid of it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T08:53:53-08:00","id":391476,"title":"","content":"Vampire 2e's justification for the vulnerability to fire is purely metaphorical, but for the most part fire seems to serve a similar role in existing vampire lore to what it does in the battle against the Lernean Hydra: as a follow-up process to ensure that the thing doesn't keep restoring itself in short order.<br /> <br /> A Promethean is a complex balance of internal processes run by a phenomenon that resonates with anything that can be used as a power source. Fire is a notoriously and overtly dangerous instance of such things. Hang a circuitboard or a wire sculpture over an open flame and see how good it looks or how well it works after a swing through the part you're not supposed to touch.<br /> <br /> So much of the Pilgrimage is about refinement, about building ever-finer connections to one's potential humanity. Fine things burn notoriously rapidly. It's why kindling is the size that it is. In particular contrast, the Zeky run on an instance of the Divine Fire that's resonant with slow nonfunctional mutation at its most common levels and regular Prometheans restore themselves with a force associated with some of the finest and most complex devices in the world.<br /> <br /> Both of those forces can also burn you, but that's not their <i>primary manifestation of power.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T10:24:48-08:00","id":391613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/390048-2e-thoughts-do-we-need-the-vulnerability-to-fire?p=391171#post391171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Prometheans aren\u2019t like that, necessarily: they may not be \u201cdead things\u201d. They eat and breathe, and I wouldn\u2019t be surprised to learn that they have a pulse. Arguably, they shouldn\u2019t benefit from \u201call damage is bashing\u201d: unlike the undead, it\u2019s entirely possible that their internal organs actually <i>do something</i> \u2014 though probably not what they would do if the Promethean was human. For instance, the stomache digests food \u2014 but in the case of a Promethean, this \u201cdigestion\u201d is more of a metaphysical furnace feeding the Azoth that drives the Promethean. The lungs probably work in a similar way, feeding the Fire instead of oxygenating the blood. In effect, a Promethean\u2019s body is an intricate alchemical engine that drives its ongoing animation; and if any of its parts get damaged, that likely throws the alchemical reactions out of whack. So swords and bullets do lethal rather than bashing.<br /> <br /> If this is so, then special vulnerability to fire isn\u2019t appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>This description really makes me want to crack open a Promethean and help me learn how they tick... I hope 2e talks about physical vs. metaphysical organs/bits/furnaces. As for my own thoughts on the subject, if anyone's read Alan Moore's Swamp Thing, the issue &quot;The Anatomy Lesson&quot; was a big inspiration for my Simulacre alternative Morality rules.<br /> <br /> But I digress!<br /> <br /> I don't think anyone here is arguing that fire shouldn't hurt, just that it shouldn't automatically deal aggravated damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T04:41:50-08:00","id":393649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/390048-2e-thoughts-do-we-need-the-vulnerability-to-fire?p=391476#post391476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Promethean is a complex balance of internal processes run by a phenomenon that resonates with ahnything that can be used as a power source. Fire is a notoriously and overtly dangerous instance of such things. Hang a circuitboard or a wire sculpture over an open flame and see how good it looks or how well it works after a swing through the part you're not supposed to touch.</div> </div> </div> </div> if this is a rationale for fire as a bane, i could argue the same thing for running a ton of electricity through a Prommie to overload their circuit. But... They heal instead. High amounts of unregulated electricity , freezing cold, acid, sledgehammers... All of them are great at destroying fine things like circuit boards. <br /> <br /> On the matter... Electricity healing golems and marble statues is a bit... Odd. Make no mistake, this is all tied to Frankenstein's Monster. The fire, the electricity. Its iconic for his story. Fire bad, lightning giving life. Everything else is nothing more tahn in story justification after the fact; its simplicity within itself to come up with justifications for any mechanic you want. Mary Shelley's story is the primary drive here. Which is a bit of a strain, when you get to it.<br /> <br /> Frankie is both the entire gameline, and a single splat within it. That lineage is fire aligned. The others are aligned to other elements - why is everyone so affected with flames and electricity, and not water or earth? This leads to an internal dissonance within the game. I vote for removing the &quot;everyone is part Frankie&quot; parts to make a more inclusive Created Beings game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T09:19:22-08:00","id":393839,"title":"","content":"Fire's not as directed a force as electricity, and from philosophical and alchemical perspective has more destructive (entropic) properties than electricity. Lightning is associated with the heavens more often than fire directly, tying into the New Dawn. Electricity is a higher order of power in terms of mastery and use than fire, and Prometheans being based on that means that lesser channels for the Divine Fire are like poison(Which would explain why the Zeka heal from nuclear energy rather than electric).<br /> <br /> There's a number of reasons why fire, a baser channel for the Divine Fire, wouldn't do it for the Prometheans who evoke some pretty high end concepts. At the root may be Frankenstein, but the idea branches out to a lot of other ideas that strengthen the narrative in it's alchemical, modern psuedo-scientific(electricity as elan vital, for example), and philosophical. Fire also has it's roots in Frankenstein but does much the same thing.<br /> <br /> I think, really, we need to ask what reasons beyond Frankenstein was fire made a weakness before saying we need to get rid of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T09:30:47-08:00","id":393861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/390048-2e-thoughts-do-we-need-the-vulnerability-to-fire?p=393649#post393649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> if this is a rationale for fire as a bane, i could argue the same thing for running a ton of electricity through a Prommie to overload their circuit.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, because as I literally <i>ended that post by saying</i>\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Both of those forces can also burn you, but that's not their </span><i>primary manifestation of power.</i> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The others are aligned to other elements - why is everyone so affected with flames and electricity, and not water or earth? </div> </div> </div>Because symbolically the other three classics are both nigh-omnipresent and not possessed of <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heraclitus#Hodos_ano_kato.2C_.22the_way_up_and_the_way_down.22\" target=\"_blank\">t</a><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heraclitus#Hodos_ano_kato.2C_.22the_way_up_and_the_way_down.22\" target=\"_blank\">he</a> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Empedocles#Philosophy\" target=\"_blank\">s</a><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Empedocles#Philosophy\" target=\"_blank\">ame</a> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theft_of_fire\" target=\"_blank\">t</a><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theft_of_fire\" target=\"_blank\">hematic</a> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fire_(classical_element)#Greek_and_Roman_tradition\" target=\"_blank\">w</a><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fire_(classical_element)#Greek_and_Roman_tradition\" target=\"_blank\">eight</a> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galvanism\" target=\"_blank\">a</a><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galvanism\" target=\"_blank\">s</a> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electrolysis\" target=\"_blank\">f</a><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electrolysis\" target=\"_blank\">ire</a> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bioelectromagnetics\" target=\"_blank\">a</a><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bioelectromagnetics\" target=\"_blank\">nd</a> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electrotherapy\" target=\"_blank\">electricity.</a><br /> <br /> Also because that's a terrible twee application of elemental theory. Prometheans are not Pok\u00e9mon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-05-2015, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T09:37:41-08:00","id":393866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/390048-2e-thoughts-do-we-need-the-vulnerability-to-fire?p=393861#post393861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also because that's a terrible twee application of elemental theory. Prometheans are not Pok\u00e9mon.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Verney, I choose you!&quot;<br /> &quot;...&quot;<br /> &quot;...&quot;<br /> *Crackles slightly*<br /> &quot;I'll be going now.&quot;<br /> &quot;You do that.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T10:49:50-08:00","id":393968,"title":"","content":"The rationale given in 1e for why fire burns Prometheans so much worse than it does mortals is nice, but not essential: that is, the writers of 2e shouldn\u2019t choose to keep the vulnerability to fire in order to preserve that explanation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T13:51:19-08:00","id":394091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/390048-2e-thoughts-do-we-need-the-vulnerability-to-fire?p=393968#post393968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rationale given in 1e for why fire burns Prometheans so much worse than it does mortals is nice, but not essential: that is, the writers of 2e shouldn\u2019t choose to keep the vulnerability to fire in order to preserve that explanation.</div> </div> </div> </div>But there is just something iconic about mobs hunting down the Prometheans with fires and pitchforks.<br /> <br /> Or for the modern mob, molotov cocktail and baseball bats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T14:42:05-08:00","id":394129,"title":"","content":"Oh, certainly. But should pitchforks do aggravated damage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T17:27:50-08:00","id":394298,"title":"","content":"Exactly. That's it exactly. <br /> <br /> I do feel like Promethean could introduce some alchemist cocktails that are anathema to the Created, though. Some kind of universal solvent. Maybe it does aggravated damage to everything given the folkloric origins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T18:00:02-08:00","id":394308,"title":"","content":"Now I'm curious what it'd be like to have alcohol as the Promethean bane.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey Charlie, want some beer?&quot; &quot;No thanks.&quot; &quot;Everyone else is.&quot; [everyone glowers helpfully] &quot;Fine.&quot; &quot;We are going to watch you drink it. It's how we know you're one of us.&quot; &quot;...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T18:08:23-08:00","id":394313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/390048-2e-thoughts-do-we-need-the-vulnerability-to-fire?p=394129#post394129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, certainly. But should pitchforks do aggravated damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pitchforks weren't the weapon of choice when it came time to hunt down the Thing.<br /> <br /> Prometheans aren't the only Created in the game, y'all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T21:06:36-08:00","id":394417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/390048-2e-thoughts-do-we-need-the-vulnerability-to-fire?p=394298#post394298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do feel like Promethean could introduce some alchemist cocktails that are anathema to the Created, though. Some kind of universal solvent. Maybe it does aggravated damage to everything given the folkloric origins.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think interesting would to see that each Linage has different Bane And Healing, based on Element it's govered. Let's leave the Frankenstein with Bane of Fire and Healing by Lighting. But let's give the Nephri Bane of Ice and Healing by Water ( best by the Rivers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), Galateids Bane of Storm ( or maybe Disese? ) and Healing by the Wind ( best the Logos, cities talk ), Tammuzes Bane of Mud and Healing by the Earth ( by burying oneself in it ) and Ulgans Bane of Corpus ( of Ghosts ans Spirits ) and Healing by the Ephemera. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T08:52:54-08:00","id":394943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/390048-2e-thoughts-do-we-need-the-vulnerability-to-fire?p=393839#post393839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think, really, we need to ask what reasons beyond Frankenstein was fire made a weakness before saying we need to get rid of it.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's just it. There isn't one. Its thematic for Frankenstein. Its not thematic for others.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/390048-2e-thoughts-do-we-need-the-vulnerability-to-fire?p=393861#post393861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, because as I literally <i>ended that post by saying</i>\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div> And I disagree with you. My problem is that your rationale has holes large enough to run a steam engine train through them. You are dismissing electricity's properties that don't fit your theory.<br /> <br /> The primary manifestation of electricity throughout history is an uncontrolled, undirected, unregulated lightning bolt. You can't use that to power &quot;<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">some of the finest and most complex devices in the world.&quot; Go back in time a bit (like with a Dark Eras setting!) and suddenly, your argument doesn't even exist yet.<br /> <br /> Take one of your fine device from America to Europe. Don't use an adapter, plug it into a wall. What happens? A short out, not enough power, something fries... Destruction. Electricity is only safe so long as it is carefully controlled and regulated. Same with fire, really. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because symbolically the other three classics are both nigh-omnipresent and not possessed of <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heraclitus#Hodos_ano_kato.2C_.22the_way_up_and_the_way_down.22\" target=\"_blank\">t</a><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heraclitus#Hodos_ano_kato.2C_.22the_way_up_and_the_way_down.22\" target=\"_blank\">he</a> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Empedocles#Philosophy\" target=\"_blank\">s</a><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Empedocles#Philosophy\" target=\"_blank\">ame</a> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theft_of_fire\" target=\"_blank\">t</a><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theft_of_fire\" target=\"_blank\">hematic</a> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fire_(classical_element)#Greek_and_Roman_tradition\" target=\"_blank\">w</a><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fire_(classical_element)#Greek_and_Roman_tradition\" target=\"_blank\">eight</a> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galvanism\" target=\"_blank\">a</a><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galvanism\" target=\"_blank\">s</a> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electrolysis\" target=\"_blank\">f</a><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electrolysis\" target=\"_blank\">ire</a> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bioelectromagnetics\" target=\"_blank\">a</a><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bioelectromagnetics\" target=\"_blank\">nd</a> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electrotherapy\" target=\"_blank\">electricity.</a><br /> <br /> Also because that's a terrible twee application of elemental theory. Prometheans are not Pok\u00e9mon. </div> </div> </div> Missing the point. 1e associated each Promethean with an element. And yet, for some reason, they were all also associated with fire? Where is the association with these other elements, if everyone is so tied to Fire?<br /> <br /> The point is that it <i>doesn't make sense</i>. Its contradictory.<br /> <br /> If you want to go with alchemical properties* as a reason, then acid should work as well. Known in alchemy as &quot;universal solvent.&quot; Acid has plenty scientific and thematic weight as well.<br /> <br /> All those links you gave? All that are part of the pseudo-science that Mary Shelly used to give Frankenstein life. Its irrevocably tied into the Frankenstein mythos... but Promethean contains more than just Frankenstein's monster. Gallatea were given the Divine Breath. Osiris has the Water of Life. Golems (and thus the Tammuz) were brought to life with the inscribed word for Truth. You can't tell me that those don't have a ton of thematic weight in stories, philosophy, and mythology. They do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It all keeps linking back to the fact that there's no strong reason for Fire to be a bane and electricity to be a healing agent beyond &quot;Fire Bad!&quot; and &quot;Its AALLLLIIIIIIVVVVVEEEEE!&quot; Any link to some philosophy or myth in favor is countered by Promethean's own references within the non-Frankenstein Lineages.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, and while we're on the subject of &quot;twee elemental theory?&quot; You do realize that twee theory is how alchemists justified cures for diseases and the like, right? If you have in influx of too much of one humor, you need its opposite to balance it out. So, hey! Part of the underlying game's alchemy. In 1e, that twee theory was also the justification for same-Lineage-in-throng mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T08:56:10-08:00","id":394954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/390048-2e-thoughts-do-we-need-the-vulnerability-to-fire?p=394943#post394943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's just it. There isn't one. Its thematic for Frankenstein. Its not thematic for others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone wasn't paying attention.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T10:38:42-08:00","id":395104,"title":"","content":"<b>*Cough*</b> A Promethean's Demiuge/Promethean creator &quot;steals&quot; the Divine FIRE to enliven all types of Prometheans, they just use a different elemental medium to do so <b>*Cough*</b><br /> <br /> Ahem...<br /> <br /> Basically, all Prometheans run of the same power source at the end of the day regardless of their elemental conduit. The Divine Fire reacts rather poorly with its base representation on the materiel plane, namely normal fire when the two interact. Hence the &quot;overcharge&quot; effect that normal fire has on Prometheans that causes them to take aggravated.<br /> <br /> Yes the inspiration for all this is tied to Frankenstiens ideas about man overstepping his bounds and stealing knowledge he was not supposed to have. Likewise, its to do with the fact that Adam was afraid of fire. Is that all there is to it for Promethean though?<br /> <br /> No.<br /> <br /> As I've mentioned above there is a deeper metaphysical reason presented within Prometheans source material (the interaction between the Divine Fire/Azoth in a Promethean and mundane fire).<br /> <br /> After all, pretty much all supernatural banes that cause agg across the game lines have a metaphysical underpinning within the games setting. Promethean is no different. In second edition Vampire, fire is theorized to cause agg because its specifically a tool that humans have created to banish the darkness, an element that the Kindred (and Strix) are closely tied to. Its got more to do with that then &quot;because vampires have dry skin&quot;, which is a conceit more from Masquerade/1st Edition Requiem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T13:07:43-08:00","id":395278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/390048-2e-thoughts-do-we-need-the-vulnerability-to-fire?p=394943#post394943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and while we're on the subject of &quot;twee elemental theory?&quot; You do realize that twee theory is how alchemists justified cures for diseases and the like, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do I need to point out the difference between &quot;this thing is symbolically aligned with the elemental concept of fire in this metaphysical framework&quot; and &quot;Fire deals double damage to this monster because of its type but its ability lets it heal from electric attacks&quot;?<br /> <br /> Literally any time I use the phrase &quot;twee&quot; with regard to ideas about elemental forces I'm referring to the shallow conception of a set of metaphysical elements as JRPG type-charts and fire-hates-water and what-about-wood-and-metal and other arguments that stop at the literal names of the symbols.<br /> <br /> It also really doesn't do you any favors when you call a definite chemical process like electrolysis &quot;pseudoscience.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T16:09:51-08:00","id":395545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/390048-2e-thoughts-do-we-need-the-vulnerability-to-fire?p=395104#post395104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>*Cough*</b> A Promethean's Demiuge/Promethean creator &amp;quot;steals&amp;quot; the Divine FIRE to enliven all types of Prometheans, they just use a different elemental medium to do so <b>*Cough*</b><br /> <br /> Ahem...<br /> <br /> Basically, all Prometheans run of the same power source at the end of the day regardless of their elemental conduit. The Divine Fire reacts rather poorly with its base representation on the materiel plane, namely normal fire when the two interact. Hence the &amp;quot;overcharge&amp;quot; effect that normal fire has on Prometheans that causes them to take aggravated.<br /> <br /> Yes the inspiration for all this is tied to Frankenstiens ideas about man overstepping his bounds and stealing knowledge he was not supposed to have. Likewise, its to do with the fact that Adam was afraid of fire. Is that all there is to it for Promethean though?<br /> <br /> No.<br /> <br /> As I've mentioned above there is a deeper metaphysical reason presented within Prometheans source material (the interaction between the Divine Fire/Azoth in a Promethean and mundane fire).<br /> <br /> After all, pretty much all supernatural banes that cause agg across the game lines have a metaphysical underpinning within the games setting. Promethean is no different. In second edition Vampire, fire is theorized to cause agg because its specifically a tool that humans have created to banish the darkness, an element that the Kindred (and Strix) are closely tied to. Its got more to do with that then &amp;quot;because vampires have dry skin&amp;quot;, which is a conceit more from Masquerade/1st Edition Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div>All true (and you should really get that cough looked at). From my perspective though, the question isn\u2019t whether 1e has solid metaphysical underpinnings for the vulnerability to fire; it\u2019s whether 2e should keep them. First and foremost, Promethean is a game; and the metaphysics exist to support good gameplay. So start with the question, \u201cdoes the vulnerability to fire bring enough to the gameplay experience to make it worth keeping in 2e?\u201d If the answer is yes, keep 1e\u2019s talk of fire overcharging Prometheans and thus causing aggravated damage; but if the answer is no, you can just as easily jettison that talk with no harm done. That\u2019s what I meant earlier when I said it was nice but not essential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T08:46:01-08:00","id":396399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/390048-2e-thoughts-do-we-need-the-vulnerability-to-fire?p=395545#post395545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First and foremost, Promethean is a game; and the metaphysics exist to support good gameplay. So start with the question, \u201cdoes the vulnerability to fire bring enough to the gameplay experience to make it worth keeping in 2e?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>While this is thread derailment slightly, I don't necessarily agree with this statement. For me good metaphysics is necessary for an interesting setting and a constant world. Then again, I look at it from a less &quot;game&quot; sort of view and more of a &quot;novel/book&quot; point of view. That's just me however. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T10:13:39-08:00","id":396461,"title":"","content":"I take Data's side on that one, but metaphysical consistency is the second question I ask after &quot;Is this interesting for the game?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T15:37:50-08:00","id":396859,"title":"","content":"Likewise. It\u2019s just that the \u201cfire causes an overload and thus aggravated damage\u201d thing feels less like an essential bit of metaphysical consistency than \u201cwe want fire to do aggravated damage to Prometheans; what bit of metaphysics could we use to justify that?\u201d Nice, but not something that would get me up in arms if it were dropped. So for this particular topic, the metaphysical explanation for the aggravated damage holds especially little sway with me \u2014 I don\u2019t <i>object</i> to it; but I don\u2019t think it should be the deciding factor as to whether or not fire does aggravated damage in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T22:25:23-08:00","id":397208,"title":"","content":"You could come up with an in-fiction explanation for anything. Prometheans could have a vulnerability to bagels because the Divine Fire had a bad time in New York City once. What really matters is how it affects gameplay and theme. In this case, it really feels unnecessary and largely pointless on both ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T22:49:38-08:00","id":397221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/390048-2e-thoughts-do-we-need-the-vulnerability-to-fire?p=397208#post397208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could come up with an in-fiction explanation for anything. Prometheans could have a vulnerability to bagels because the Divine Fire had a bad time in New York City once. What really matters is how it affects gameplay and theme. In this case, it really feels unnecessary and largely pointless on both ends.</div> </div> </div> </div>The words &quot;pointless&quot; and &quot;unnecessary&quot; were redefined for me this week when an elemental force of transformation-destruction-and-renewal was equated with farming implements and breakfast foods in symbolic weight.<br /> <br /> You're not adding to your argument by doing this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T00:36:02-08:00","id":397268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/390048-2e-thoughts-do-we-need-the-vulnerability-to-fire?p=396859#post396859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likewise. It\u2019s just that the \u201cfire causes an overload and thus aggravated damage\u201d thing feels less like an essential bit of metaphysical consistency than \u201cwe want fire to do aggravated damage to Prometheans; what bit of metaphysics could we use to justify that?\u201d Nice, but not something that would get me up in arms if it were dropped. So for this particular topic, the metaphysical explanation for the aggravated damage holds especially little sway with me \u2014 I don\u2019t <i>object</i> to it; but I don\u2019t think it should be the deciding factor as to whether or not fire does aggravated damage in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok that's interesting. Mainly because we get into meta-stuff that is basically a chicken and the egg argument right?<br /> <br /> Your saying that the dev's went in with the idea that fire should do agg (lets say because Adam was afraid of fire in Frankenstein) and back engineered a reason why this was the case.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking that the original dev (Bill Bridges?) came up with a game idea, a rough setting and such and decided while he was working out his metaphysics that fire should do aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> I guess we'll never really know without picking the original developers brain, however, as with most things the truth is probably more complex and lies somewhere in the middle. <br /> <br /> However, if we are not doing to use the games own internal rational/metaphysics as a reason to decide if a feature should be in or outside the game, then we are left purely out of game reasons to decide if such a feature should be in the game. Which leaves us with the &quot;fun factor&quot; (bah...humbug I say) of having Fire be extra dangerous or not or the more narrative idea of:<br /> <br /> &quot;What does having Fire do aggravated damage add to the game?&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't really know how to answer that in a concise way and I think it will be different for every Promethean game. For me a metaphysical explanation is all that really needed, but once again I acknowledge I'm a bit odd in this particular area.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T02:19:56-08:00","id":397296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/390048-2e-thoughts-do-we-need-the-vulnerability-to-fire?p=397268#post397268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok that's interesting. Mainly because we get into meta-stuff that is basically a chicken and the egg argument right?<br /> <br /> Your saying that the dev's went in with the idea that fire should do agg (lets say because Adam was afraid of fire in Frankenstein) and back engineered a reason why this was the case.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking that the original dev (Bill Bridges?) came up with a game idea, a rough setting and such and decided while he was working out his metaphysics that fire should do aggravated damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda, but not really; I\u2019m not presuming to know what went through the original developers\u2019 heads. Let\u2019s try this a different way: let\u2019s say that 2e was already out and you were looking at it with fresh eyes (that is, without ever having read he first edition), and there was no mention anywhere of fire causing aggravated damage to Prometheans. Would you even notice? <br /> <br /> I guess what I\u2019m trying to say is that I like metaphysical consistency; but in this case, we\u2019ll have metaphysical consistency <i>either way</i>: if they choose to keep the \u201cfire does aggravated\u201d, they\u2019ve got a metaphysical explanation for it; if they choose to ditch the \u201cfire does aggravated\u201d, they can drop that bit of metaphysical explanation from the game without leaving any holes in the overall metaphysics. So in this case, the decision can be made strictly on the basis of the gameplay experience without reference to metaphysics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T06:49:13-08:00","id":397498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Hawthorn:</b> Your saying that the dev's went in with the idea that fire should do agg (lets say because Adam was afraid of fire in Frankenstein) </div> </div> </div>Point of pedantry: the Creature was not named Adam, either by Frankenstein or himself (he says he should have been Frankenstein's Adam, but never takes the name). <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [b]Dataweaver: So in this case, the decision can be made strictly on the basis of the gameplay experience without reference to metaphysics. </div> </div> </div>True. Personally, I think the vulnerability is unnecessary; and as I said earlier, I think a better mechanism for a bane would be to leech Pyros rather than do damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T15:52:56-07:00","id":512377,"title":"","content":"One of things that really never made sense to me about the fire vulnerability aspect is it really wasn't even much of a thing in the Frankenstein book. The Monster's only interactions with fire was one incident in which he burned himself trying to warm himself. (And that's framed more as not knowing that fire was painful than anything else.) and that he intended to ignite himself in order to kill himself at the end of the book. Otherwise he appeared to have little problem with fire.<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell the &quot;fire bad!&quot; element can almost entirely be traced back to the 1931 Boris Karloff movie, where the monster expresses a profound fear of fire. (Though that interpretation is very different from the book)<br /> <br /> But yes, I agree that Prometheans could use a different bane. (I do think they could use one, if only because it seems thematically appropriate for something so resilient to have some sort of weak spot. I'd also prefer different ways to channel Pyros based on lineage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5823-ravian3","name":"Ravian3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T00:59:37-07:00","id":512713,"title":"","content":"Why not make them more vulnerable during torment? <br /> <br /> It's a massive incentive not to abuse it, or slip up and fall into it. <br /> <br /> That's why fire did more damage to Frankie, he was in torment. <br /> <br /> Also, as the divine fire animates *all* of the created (even the Unfleshed, and Zeko) they should *all* share the same vulnerability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5544-ancientswordrage","name":"AncientSwordRage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T08:13:39-07:00","id":512928,"title":"","content":"Mediums matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T08:30:59-07:00","id":512937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/390048-2e-thoughts-do-we-need-the-vulnerability-to-fire?p=512928#post512928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mediums matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Short Mediums at large?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5544-ancientswordrage","name":"AncientSwordRage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T08:34:26-07:00","id":512938,"title":"","content":"More news tonight at 10.<br /> <br /> I might elaborate what I meant later today. Maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T09:09:48-07:00","id":512971,"title":"","content":"Throwing in my 2 cents here.<br /> <br /> Been a while since I played Promethean, since I generally lean towards Mage. That said, the theme in 1e, which seems to being pulled even more into the setting of 2e, is Alchemy. Everything makes reference to the different precepts, from the 4 elements (plus spiritual quintessence) as the basic character types, the classic metals as the refinements, the concept of Magnum Opus, and so on. Sure, you could ascribe this to the Prometheans fitting Alchemy on to their journey (I.e. They ascribed the concepts of Alchemy, rather than their basis be derived from it) but the themes of the game itself ascribe to the idea of Alchemy being the central basis (just as Mage draws on Plato's Theory of Forms and Kaballah, along with other mystical traditions).<br /> <br /> The thing is, Alchemy is essentially a mystical science of reactions and processes (there is a reason it helped form the basis of what became modern chemistry). In Promethean, considering the strong theme of Alechemy within the setting, would it be going to far in saying that certain elements react in different ways, not because of what they are scientifically, but instead by their alchemical definitions? I mean, if you want to get into science, I could ask how a man restores life to a corpse he submerged in water, cut into 13 pieces of which he then sewed 12 of those pieces back together, spit on and then made eat rose petals while breathing mystical life into them? I am not saying this to be facetious, but to point out that mystical and symbolic processes are the basis of the games setting. <br /> <br /> Thus, fire and Promethean flesh not mixing well is another of those processes, regardless of whether you justify it as the flaring of the Pyros, to it preventing regeneration(a la trolls and hydras) or dead flesh burns easier (a la vampires. <br /> <br /> I always liked to apply Mage logic* of &quot;everything is a symbol&quot;: Electricity heals as it Symbolically a source of energy, recharging, and power that is controlled (even Lightning was ascribed to gods being angry), while fire harms because it is symbolically a force of cleansing,destructive renewal that is at most contained but never fully controlled. Or, as my player (an Obrimos Adamantine arrow) put it when describing how to fight Prometheans: &quot;when you start to die, we give you an electric shock with paddles**. When we want you to die, we set you on fire. Same principle works on these guys, just with a bit more oomph.&quot;<br /> <br /> *and like all Mage logic, I am sure that while trying to explain everything, I am at least off point if not completely wrong <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> ** yes, I know even that electricity can kill if used improperly(I am an MD), but it is fun way to think about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 05-13-2015, 12:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T09:45:29-07:00","id":513004,"title":"","content":"I'm of the opinion that fire is destructive to Prometheans not because it represents destruction (because Fire and Lightning have very similar symbolism here, actually), but because it is unrefined. Electricity, nowadays at least, can be considered to be a symbol of human mastery over nature, the triumph of mortal wills of natural forces, much like fire once was, but where fire is wild and unrefined, electricity is &quot;purer&quot; and more abstract. I hope I'm making sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T14:29:44-07:00","id":514490,"title":"","content":"Fire bad.<br /> <br /> Really, it ought to be that simple. Forget the non-explanation of 1e; Prometheans are corpses infused with volatile chemicals and/or stuffed with dead plant matter, or machinery coated in oil now apparently. Fire as an inhibitor of regeneration also dates back at least to Greek myth (Hail Hydra!), which sets it up as a viable Promethean curse. The Pyros isn't fire, but is merely symbolized <i>by</i> fire, being a divine force of inspiration, disruption, and evolution. Prometheans aren't themselves crucibles, they're the materials transmuted inside, and enjoy no immunity themselves when the flames lick over the edge.<br /> <br /> There aren't many suitable alternative banes. Gold would be cool, were it not for the shenanigans it would inspire. Supernally perfected metals, or alchemical admixtures, but those are less common than gold. Lead would be great, except then guns would be more lethal to the Created than they are to humans. Eagle feathers? Acids and/or bases? Scrimshawed bones?<br /> <br /> Non-vulnerability seems inappropriate, given the central symbolism of the Pyros, but as a boon it would either be overpowered (alongside Electroshock Therapy), or counter to the pitchforks-and-torches imagery we love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T18:40:18-07:00","id":514698,"title":"","content":"I love &quot;other state of Linage Element&quot;. Ice, as frozen Water, would be Bane of Osirians. Fire, as untamed &quot;lighing&quot; (???), would kill Frankenstein's. Ghosts would be a doom of Ulgans, as &quot;dead&quot; ephemera killing &quot;living&quot; one. Those opposites would nice, would be varied, and worked with Alchemical Themes of <b>Promethean</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T21:35:58-07:00","id":514777,"title":"","content":"I like alternative banes, but perhaps with a few differences. For example Salt sounds like a better bane than ice for Osirans (being an impurity to water yet also commonly found in it) The main thing that should be taken into account is the likelihood of such banes coming into play. Fire is a substance commonly weaponized, rare alchemical substances less so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5823-ravian3","name":"Ravian3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T16:42:41-07:00","id":517402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/390048-2e-thoughts-do-we-need-the-vulnerability-to-fire?p=513004#post513004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm of the opinion that fire is destructive to Prometheans not because it represents destruction (because Fire and Lightning have very similar symbolism here, actually), but because it is unrefined. Electricity, nowadays at least, can be considered to be a symbol of human mastery over nature, the triumph of mortal wills of natural forces, much like fire once was, but where fire is wild and unrefined, electricity is &amp;quot;purer&amp;quot; and more abstract. I hope I'm making sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>That only works post industrial revolution, though. In a Dark Eras game before humankind had learned to harness electricitity, it would be the opposite. Electricity would be an uncontrollable thing only experienced via the destruction it causes during a storm, while fire would be a natural force, tamed by humans and used to bring light and heat under their control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T11:10:32-07:00","id":518318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/390048-2e-thoughts-do-we-need-the-vulnerability-to-fire?p=517402#post517402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That only works post industrial revolution, though. In a Dark Eras game before humankind had learned to harness electricitity, it would be the opposite. Electricity would be an uncontrollable thing only experienced via the destruction it causes during a storm, while fire would be a natural force, tamed by humans and used to bring light and heat under their control.</div> </div> </div> </div>This also touches on one of the other reasons I'd like alternative methods of regaining Pyros. Recharging through electricity makes dark eras games that much more difficult. For example I'm planning on doing a game during the Post-civil war reconstruction era, very thematic but it's going to be that much harder for players to maintain their Pyros. Either I throw in a lot of storms for characters to be lightning rods in, or they make do with a limited supply of Pyros each day.<br /> <br /> Once again, electricity is more of a thematic choice than a logical one. The majority of lineages don't have squat to do with electricity, and most of them even started before electricity was anything other than untamed lightning.<br /> <br /> The Sun thing is fine, its a regular supply regardless of when your game is set, and it works off the theory that the Sun is a giant battery of Pyros. The elemental healing bit also works well, particularly given how each lineage has their own way of doing it.<br /> <br /> Perhaps it might be better if Pyros was something that occurred a little more naturally, and thus could be collected by Prometheans through a variety of ways (electricity being one of them). It'd also open things up for more pyros related weirdness in the world, such as areas where Pandorans roamed without the presence of Prometheans, or other weird phenomenon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5823-ravian3","name":"Ravian3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T12:35:38-07:00","id":518381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravian3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/390048-2e-thoughts-do-we-need-the-vulnerability-to-fire?p=518318#post518318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps it might be better if Pyros was something that occurred a little more naturally, and thus could be collected by Prometheans through a variety of ways (electricity being one of them). It'd also open things up for more pyros related weirdness in the world, such as areas where Pandorans roamed without the presence of Prometheans, or other weird phenomenon.</div> </div> </div> </div>A few people have compared Pyros to Mania from Genius (the fangame), which got me thinking: Why not have Pyros be realeased into the world whenever some great moment of inspiration happens? If the Divine Fire that animates a Promethean is a brought into our reality by mankind doing the impossible, then maybe changing what's possible can bring in a little bit of Pyros?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T12:46:16-07:00","id":519891,"title":"","content":"The question is how do you implement that in terms of game mechanics. Electricity may have issues but it can generally be depended on as a consistent source in most modern settings. Same with stuff like Vitae and Glamour that can generally just come from humans without a lot of outside factors other than the supernatural. Meanwhile stuff like Essence, Manna and Aether are rarer but are derived from sites intrinsically linked to this Supernatural creature in question.<br /> <br /> Pyros is in a sort of odd halfway point. They generally state that Pyros doesn't generally exist in nature, but then try to make it easier by linking it to electricity. The mania idea has some similarities to human derived fuel sources like Vitae and Glamour, but has the issue of being rather specific. Inspiration is not something that Prometheans can easily inspire like Changelings can do with most emotions, it's rather specific.<br /> <br /> Really I can see Pyros being handled either way, but we need to consider what those ways would mean for the game.<br /> <br /> If Pyros is generated by humans, it needs to be able to occur without huge amounts of hassle. This is especially true given that Prometheans don't really do well with interacting with humans. A Promethean going out of its way to &quot;inspire&quot; a human is problematic, especially since such a method would be generally needed for more on the fly recharges (to supplement a Prometheans daily intake of Pyros)<br /> <br /> If Pyros is generated by locations, first we need to consider how it would happen, but we also need to make sure it doesn't mess with the themes involved. Prometheans are supposed to be mobile, having sources of power be static works for Werewolves tied to their territory and Mages with their domains, but it doesn't work for Prommies. If a Promethean is encouraged to hang around an area that dispenses Pyros, it means they will be distracted from their pilgrimage.<br /> <br /> <br /> Based off of this it may be better to make Pyros sites temporary as well. Let's say that general weirdness floods an area with Pyros (anything from a freak incident, a burst of inspiration from a mortal, a Quashmalin appearing, plenty of things.) This probably even has a compound effect given that the Pyros is likely to instill more inspiration in other people.<br /> <br /> This essentially creates a Pyros field in the area that attracts even more weirdness, Prommies are drawn to the area based off of its radiance, Pandorans awaken and are more resistant to dormancy, and if there's enough of the stuff it will eventually create a firestorm. It means that Prommies will generally have reasons to congregate in small numbers while still being mobile, and it also ensures that Prommies will be fairly guaranteed to end up somewhere interesting given the attraction to places where weird stuff already happens.<br /> <br /> Eventually however, the Prommies have to move on, typically due to a mixture of the end of the Pyros in the area as well as the locals collective disquiet and the growing wasteland in the area. But if the Pyros grows to high enough levels, you end up with a firestorm driving everyone out.<br /> <br /> One thing this could also mean is that some Prometheans will see an obligation to settle Pyros fields down. Left unattended, Pyros will generally have a compound effect on itself as more and more weird things come to town and the Pyros of such impossible things increases in the area until it climaxes in a firestorm. If a Promethean can deal with the crazy and calm the area, they can have some time to focus on their pilgrimage while they bask in the remaining Pyros rather than being caught in the crazy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5823-ravian3","name":"Ravian3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T20:23:43-07:00","id":532713,"title":"","content":"Salt (or other desiccants) for Water, corrosives for Earth, smoke/poison gas for Air? No idea for Spirit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T16:37:45-07:00","id":533759,"title":"","content":"Hmm... spirits generally have their own personal banes. Unless there's a specific substance that all spirits dislike, perhaps Ulgans would pick up a more specific bane. Possibly they could take on the banes of spirits around them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5823-ravian3","name":"Ravian3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T09:53:20-07:00","id":534512,"title":"","content":"The thing about fire is that is is very easy to weaponize for a normal, doo-da mortal. Every human being on earth, from Norway to Japan, from 16 to 61, has access to fire. It is the founding technology of humanity. This means it's very easy for any mortal to be able to discover the Promethean's weakness, and become a threat.<br /> <br /> A small-town sheriff holds a bandaged Ulgan at bay using a homemade torch. &quot;Don't move, or I'll burn you!&quot; It's a simple scene, and easy to picture. It also relates back to the audience, because having fire in your face is legit scary. Now if that Ulgan's bane has to be gold, things start to get complicated. How did they discover that? And how is the sheriff suppose to weaponize that without some ludicrous explanation? If the weakness is ghosts, than there really isn't a way short of some goofy Ghostbusters bullshit.<br /> <br /> Remember, Prometheans are highly uncommon. If their weaknesses are too varied or too weird, most of their potential enemies aren't going to know about it. The random chance someone in a mob is going to set something on fire is way higher than that they will be carrying gold bullets or ghost grenades.<br /> <br /> Symbolically, fire is the friend of man. Pretty much all of our technology stems from it. Arguably use of fire is what makes us human, and fire being the bane of Prometheans is just one more thing that says to them that they are definitively not-human.<br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> As far as underlying physical reasons are concerned, I'd say it's because Prometheans are largely unstable alchemical reactions, and their forms just react violently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T11:22:28-07:00","id":534627,"title":"","content":"Yeah but Prometheans are also creations of man. Hell they're even powered by the &quot;Divine Fire&quot;, fire makes sense for vampires since they are actual predators of humanity (not to mention the whole fire is the sun controlled by humans idea.)<br /> <br /> But Prometheans are essentially described as vessels of divine fire, and it becomes nonsensical for electricity to empower them while fire burns them to a crisp.<br /> <br /> I agree that we need to keep in mind that the substance be possible to weaponize, but consider that Werewolves are weak to silver, a substance notoriously useless as a material for weapons. (To the point where the new book makes it clear a silver weapon will take serious penalties in regular combat while a silver coated one will only be good for one hit.) Changeling also has a similar bit with Cold Iron (A notoriously brittle and fragile version of regular iron.)<br /> <br /> The only reasons these substances were chosen over something more useful was because they were thematically appropriate enough to be commonly used. (Even a human who has no experience with werewolves can make a guess based on pop culture to bring silver if he believes a werewolf is hunting him, the cold Iron takes a tad more research (iron fearing fey creatures aren't as common in pop culture) but changelings are appropriately less dangerous than a raging werewolf.)<br /> <br /> In addition these creatures also have clearly logical reasons why they'd have such weaknesses. Werewolves have the connection to Luna, who's connected to silver. Changelings have numerous justifications for cold iron to choose from (generally either iron is symbolic of the mundane and thus the antithesis of faerie or because the True Fae broke a contract with the very concept of Iron.)<br /> <br /> Vampires' fire weakness fits all three categories of thematic, easily weaponized and logical.<br /> <br /> <br /> Prometheans' fire weakness is easily weaponized, but is only thematic when considering the Boris Karloff movie (again, Frankenstein's monster had very little problem with fire, it burned him once (that tends to happen to most people when they stick their hands in it.) he shows no subsequent dislike of fire and the book concludes with the implied ending that the monster commits suicide via self immolation.) Furthermore its anti-logical. Prometheans aren't undead like vampires, and are even stated to be powered by a fire-like substance that's transmitted by a source of energy that typically results in fire as well. (and again the lightning connection is only really thematic to Frankenstein as well, the other lineages have nothing to do with electricity.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5823-ravian3","name":"Ravian3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T11:57:18-07:00","id":534656,"title":"","content":"Werewolves weaknesses are also well-known...almost everyone should know about silver. Changelings are rarer and cold-iron supposedly harder to use (cold iron varies from being uncommon to ridiculously common depending on time and place) but changelings are nowhere near as durable as vampires, werewolves, or Prometheans. Changelings' primary antagonists will also typically not be mortals who need to exploit a weakness, but Fae and their agents who know about it. Likewise werewolves primary antagonists are going to be spirits and other werewolves. There are not enough Prometheans to allow for the primary antagonist of Prometheans to be other Created, and the number of intelligent Pandorans is equally rare. The second edition even seems to be gearing up for humans to be a bigger overall threat.<br /> <br /> If Prometheans are fueled by the Divine Fire, perhaps it simply doesn't react well with more fire. Maybe you shouldn't feed it, how about that? There are lots of reasons setting something on fire might be bad besides dead flesh being easier to burn.<br /> <br /> Interestingly you mention the Boris Karloff film, but silver as weakness for werewolves really doesn't appear all that much earlier, and largely seems an invention of another Universal monster film.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T12:58:13-07:00","id":534732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravian3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/390048-2e-thoughts-do-we-need-the-vulnerability-to-fire?p=534627#post534627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but Prometheans are also creations of man. Hell they're even powered by the &quot;Divine Fire&quot;, fire makes sense for vampires since they are actual predators of humanity (not to mention the whole fire is the sun controlled by humans idea.)<br /> <br /> But Prometheans are essentially described as vessels of divine fire, and it becomes nonsensical for electricity to empower them while fire burns them to a crisp.<br /> <br /> I agree that we need to keep in mind that the substance be possible to weaponize, but consider that Werewolves are weak to silver, a substance notoriously useless as a material for weapons. (To the point where the new book makes it clear a silver weapon will take serious penalties in regular combat while a silver coated one will only be good for one hit.) Changeling also has a similar bit with Cold Iron (A notoriously brittle and fragile version of regular iron.)<br /> <br /> The only reasons these substances were chosen over something more useful was because they were thematically appropriate enough to be commonly used. (Even a human who has no experience with werewolves can make a guess based on pop culture to bring silver if he believes a werewolf is hunting him, the cold Iron takes a tad more research (iron fearing fey creatures aren't as common in pop culture) but changelings are appropriately less dangerous than a raging werewolf.)<br /> <br /> In addition these creatures also have clearly logical reasons why they'd have such weaknesses. Werewolves have the connection to Luna, who's connected to silver. Changelings have numerous justifications for cold iron to choose from (generally either iron is symbolic of the mundane and thus the antithesis of faerie or because the True Fae broke a contract with the very concept of Iron.)<br /> <br /> Vampires' fire weakness fits all three categories of thematic, easily weaponized and logical.<br /> <br /> <br /> Prometheans' fire weakness is easily weaponized, but is only thematic when considering the Boris Karloff movie (again, Frankenstein's monster had very little problem with fire, it burned him once (that tends to happen to most people when they stick their hands in it.) he shows no subsequent dislike of fire and the book concludes with the implied ending that the monster commits suicide via self immolation.) Furthermore its anti-logical. Prometheans aren't undead like vampires, and are even stated to be powered by a fire-like substance that's transmitted by a source of energy that typically results in fire as well. (and again the lightning connection is only really thematic to Frankenstein as well, the other lineages have nothing to do with electricity.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The made of something means you shouldn't be harmed by it is bollocks. We are 50-60% water. I can be drowned though, and even drinking too much water is toxic(the purer the worst it is, actually). And humans have long used tools to destroy tools, even if they are associated (last I checked, we can even use fire to stop fires, never mind using steel toils to dismantle other steel tools, such as a compactor versus a car).<br /> <br /> But, never mind thos issues. Prometheans are, at their heart, reanimated corpses that are created using different alchemical processes, which have no true logical basis due to their nature as fictional creations (that defy natural laws). As long as an internally consistent explanation is given, it is valid within their work. Most splats are dependent on the lore of the setting for the explanation, not real world lore (silver, historically, was not associated with Werewolves, but the undead). The books offer in setting explanations for weaknesses (luna and silver), which are just as justified in a fictional setting as saying that crude fire mixing with divine fire reacts poorly for the host of the Divine Fire. Any other justifications are just icing (fire prevents regeneration), but at heart, saying &quot;these are creatures crafted from alchemy, and thus certain aspects of the world react to them based on the rules of this settings alchemy, such that lighting acts this way and fire this way&quot; is all a fictional setting needs. While you can then critique the work for said choice, it doesn't mean that it is illogical or inconsistent if the material is internally consistent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 05-31-2015, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T14:49:21-07:00","id":534825,"title":"","content":"Eh... the fire vulnerability I can take or leave but I still think at the very least there should be more ways to recharge Pyros quickly than just electricity. It really makes historical games (which are honestly some of my favorite) more difficult if the only way to get some pyros back is to hope for a storm (to say nothing of the decreased utility of many of the Electrification transmutations.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5823-ravian3","name":"Ravian3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T16:02:21-07:00","id":534897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravian3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/390048-2e-thoughts-do-we-need-the-vulnerability-to-fire?p=534825#post534825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh... the fire vulnerability I can take or leave but I still think at the very least there should be more ways to recharge Pyros quickly than just electricity. It really makes historical games (which are honestly some of my favorite) more difficult if the only way to get some pyros back is to hope for a storm (to say nothing of the decreased utility of many of the Electrification transmutations.)</div> </div> </div> </div>This I agree with. If you play a historical settings, it is definitely tough to recharge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}